  "cut_point": "We are given a **5x6 grid** (i.e., 5 rows and 6 columns), which holds **30 students**. Two of these students, **A and B**, are from the **same school** and must **not be seated adjacent to each other in any direction** (up, down, left, right). We are to **count the number of seating arrangements** where A and B are not adjacent.

---

### Step 1: Total number of seating arrangements without any restrictions

We are arranging **30 students** in a **5x6 grid** (i.e., 30 seats). So the total number of ways to seat the students is:

$$
30! \quad \text{(since all students are distinguishable)}
$$",
